+// VRAM clear diagnostics (branch kext-scrubcheck). RM scrubs video memory when it is freed (PMA scrub-on-free, on by default
+// since GK110), so a fresh allocation should already read zero and the CPU clear below (~0.25 ms per MB over BAR1) would be
+// redundant. Before clearing, vramGrant reads one qword per 64 KB (one per 4 KB on every 256th grant) and counts any nonzero.
+// debug.nvrmfb_clear_mode: 2 (default) = skip the clear when every sampled qword is zero (clears with rep stosb otherwise),
+// 0 = always rep stosb (the old behaviour), 1 = movnti 64-byte lines, 3 = rep stosq. debug.nvrmfb_scrubtest=N: grant N x 8 MB, fill them with a pattern, free
+// them, grant N again and count reallocations that overlap the filled ranges / show the pattern (results in nvrmfb_scrubtest_*).
+static int gClearMode = 2;   // measured 2026-10-13: fresh grants always read zero (RM's copy-engine scrub-on-free), so the CPU clear only repeats it
